      : "Paris has conditional 60 judgments for ISR, MED, TEC and OPT, and 40 for LON. PCS, GSS and RES remain unknown, without a total centre. Actual services, licensing and operations support limited capability; historical certification and older models are not current whole-area outcomes. LON 40 concerns the reviewed disease pathway's adoption/payment gap, retaining clinical-significance and safety disputes. Regulatory caution is not itself penalised; private care, trials and other pathways are not assumed absent. Rejecting pathway relevance, net-benefit applicability or representativeness restores unknown LON. The mathematical domain is 34–74; withdrawing LON gives 30–80. Neither proves qualification or exclusion.",
