      : "Seoul has conditional 60 judgments for PCS, ISR, TEC and OPT, and 40 for LON. GSS, RES and MED remain unknown, without a total centre and with a mathematical domain of 34–74. Delivered protection, welfare connections, research transfer, digital assistance and transport support scoped capability. Actual treatment and safety monitoring at two providers are important positive evidence; waitlisting, reduced start capacity, longer waits, limited transfers and reported nonreimbursed costs and safety labour together support a material resident-access discontinuity. LON 40 still requires pathway-relevance, cost-materiality, 2025-to-2026 continuity and scope assumptions; rejection restores unknown. New evidence of affordable costs and substantive bottleneck mitigation would support reviewing 60, giving 36–76. Withdrawing LON gives 30–80; neither establishes qualification or exclusion. Return of spontaneous circulation is not discharge survival, and a single-drug bottleneck does not downgrade general medicine. September airport statistics have unverified pre-cutoff publication and are unused; seven approximate points verify neither whole boundaries nor treatment sites.",
