      : "Lisbon has conditional 60 judgments for ISR, TEC and OPT, and 40 for MED. PCS, GSS, RES and LON remain unknown, without a centre and with a mathematical domain of 27–77. MED combines actual late first consultations at multiple providers, waiting stocks and family-doctor gaps with delivered care, transfers and primary-care mitigation; completed and waiting cohorts have different denominators. Unclosed quality coding and table/prose conflicts remain, without being treated as stable mortality outcomes. An actual first-treatment statement supports LON capability, but product, payments, monitoring and ordinary resident costs are not connected. A payment query updated after the cutoff is not backfilled, and unknowns do not receive low scores. Water reserves served most customers, with local restrictions and annual interruptions retained; summaries do not prove uninterrupted service to every household. Digital parking payments account for 74% of revenue, not residents, and negotiated licences are not executed licences. Judgments require scope, continuity and material constraints after mitigation; rejection restores unknown. Withdrawing MED gives 21–86; new evidence supporting MED 60 would give 30–80. Neither establishes qualification or exclusion.",
